12	
13	// Request DTOs + parsers for the `/moderation/infractions` router. Field shapes
14	// mirror the Zod schemas in
15	// `services/api-db/src/domain/zod-schemas/validations/moderation-infractions-validations.ts`.
16	// The moderation-infractions controller wraps every parse in `captureErrors`, so
17	// a validation failure is a STRUCTURED 400 (ZOD context) — exactly like the
18	// /music + /giveaways verticals. Every failure returns the exact Zod v4.3.6
19	// message via `zodItemError` (context "ZOD", property = `issue.path.join(".")`),
20	// surfacing the FIRST failing issue.
21	//
22	// CRITICAL datetime divergence from the giveaways / kpis verticals (plan A.22):
23	// the moderation datetime fields use `z.string().datetime({ offset: true })`,
24	// which ACCEPTS a non-UTC offset (`+02:00`), UNLIKE `z.string().datetime()` /
25	// `z.iso.datetime()` (which require a literal `Z`). The regex below therefore
26	// admits `Z` OR `±HH:MM`; a failure still degrades to the shared `Invalid ISO
27	// datetime` message (same as the strict-UTC verticals).
28	//
29	// Create takes the materialized dbinfraction.CreateData (the Node repo runs a
30	// FIXED-column INSERT with `?? default`); Update builds a `map[string]any` of
31	// present columns (a present null → a nil map value → SQL NULL; absent → skipped
32	// → left unchanged; an empty map → the repo's findById fallback), reusing the
33	// track-errors / giveaways map helpers.
34	
35	// ─── enum sets + messages (zod v4 `Invalid option: expected one of ...`) ──
